issue_context.body:
Repro:
```C#
using System;
using System.IO;
using Microsoft.Win32.SafeHandles;

string path = "test.dat";
var h = File.OpenHandle("test.dat", FileMode.Create, FileAccess.ReadWrite, FileShare.None, FileOptions.DeleteOnClose);
Console.WriteLine(File.Exists(path));
h.Dispose();
Console.WriteLine(File.Exists(path));
```

This should print `true` then `false`, but on Unix it prints `true` then `true`.

Note this isn't a case of DeleteOnClose not working on Unix. It does, e.g. change the repro to use:
```C#
var h = File.Create("test.dat", 1, FileOptions.DeleteOnClose);
```
instead, and it'll correctly print out the expected results.

Rather, the code on Unix to handle emulating FileOptions.DeleteOnClose is part of FileStream.Dispose and should likely instead be a part of SafeFileHandle.

